    "description": "A square-based pyramid has a 6 m square base ABCD. The diagonals meet at O, P is directly above O, and the four congruent triangular faces have PA = PB = 11 m. Part (i) asks the student to use Pythagoras to show that OB = 3√2 m and then find the vertical height OP in surd form."
  },
