    "description": "A square-based pyramid has a 6 m square base ABCD, with P directly above the centre O, and PA = PB = 11 m. On triangular face PAB, angle PAB is 74.2 degrees to one decimal place. Part (ii) asks for the total area of the four triangular roof faces, to the nearest square metre."
  },
